  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decreasing human-elephant conflict in West Laikipia to manageable levels</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to reduce conflict between humans and elephants in Laikipia County incentral Kenya and home to Kenyas second largest elephant population. The project will separate elephants from agriculture where possible through the repair and fortification of an elephant-proof fence. Activities will include conducting outreach with residents to explain the purpose of the fence and to get buy-in and commitment necessary for long-term upkeep, improving the alignment so that wildlife-friendly properties are on one side (north and east of the fence) and incompatible agriculture is on the other side (south and west), repairing the old fence and fortifying it, establishing a fence maintenance team to prevent intentional fence destruction by people, and repair breakage where it occurs.</narrative>
  </description>
